# Technician-app mirror — the UNPACKED copy only.
#
# public/technician-mirror/<version>/ is a 14 MB working directory produced by
# `npm run export:mirror` for local dev. The Dockerfile builds its own copy from
# the tarball and deletes any committed one, so a checked-in unpacked tree would
# sit in history for nothing.
#
# mirror-app/technician-mirror-<version>.tar.gz IS committed — 4.2 MB gzipped,
# one file per app release. It is what CI feeds the Docker build context, and
# committing it is what lets a deploy produce a working mirror with no
# cross-repo token. See the `mirror` stage in Dockerfile.
/public/technician-mirror/
